{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoFiveTermArguments","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersExtend"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.extended_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.extended_sum","kind":"theorem","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L476-L492","doc":"**The level-7 sum: `Σₖ (2·L(wₖ) + L(−wₖ)) = π²/2`.**\n\n`17 + 5 - 1 = 21 = 3·7`, so the sevens cancel and the sum is `3·L(1) = π²/2`.\n\nThis is the cyclotomic-side identity the 5₂ saddle sum rule reduces to — now a\ntheorem about the corpus's own dilogarithm, given only that `x` is the root of\n`x³ - 2x² - x + 1` in `(1/2, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.extended_targets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.extended_targets","kind":"theorem","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L408-L473","doc":"**The three level-7 targets, in the form the 5₂ sum rule states them.**\n\n`E = extend (π²/6) rogersL` is the Rogers dilogarithm extended off `[0,1]` by\ninversion and Landen. The first and third roots lie outside `[0,1]`, so `E` — not\n`rogersL` — is the function these are values of.\n\nNothing about `E` is assumed: the branches unfold definitionally, and what they\nunfold to is `numerators_of_root`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.root_sub_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.root_sub_div","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L400-L405","doc":"…and the third root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.root_inv_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.root_inv_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L392-L398","doc":"`σ z = (z-1)/z` is an order-3 automorphism of the splitting field, so all\nthree roots are `x`, `1/(1-x)` and `(x-1)/x`. Here is the first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.exists_root_in_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.exists_root_in_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L370-L380","doc":"The cubic really does have a root in `(1/2, 1)`, so `numerators_of_root` is\nnot vacuous. `f(1/2) = 1/8 > 0` and `f(1) = -1 < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.numerators_of_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.numerators_of_root","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L336-L368","doc":"**The level-7 numerators `(17, 5, -1)`, from the cubic alone.**\n\nNo hypothesis about `L` remains: Abel's relation is `rogersL_fiveTerm` and\nreflection is `rogersL_one_sub`, both proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.root_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.root_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L324-L334","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.rogersL_fiveTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.rogersL_fiveTerm","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L297-L313","doc":"**Abel's five-term relation** for the Rogers dilogarithm on `(0,1)`.\n\n    L x + L y - L (x·y) - L (x(1-y)/(1-x·y)) - L (y(1-x)/(1-x·y)) = 0\n\n`L` here is `FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL`, built from the corpus's own\n`LiTwo`. This is the last hypothesis\n`FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.numerators_of_abel` takes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_abelAux_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_abelAux_zero","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L282-L293","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_inner_right_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_inner_right_zero","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L272-L280","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_inner_left_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_inner_left_zero","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L260-L270","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_mul_const_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_mul_const_zero","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L252-L258","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_rogersL_comp_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_rogersL_comp_zero","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L246-L250","doc":"An inner argument that vanishes at `0⁺` and stays positive there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_rogersL_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_rogersL_zero","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L240-L244","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_log_mul_log_one_sub_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.tendsto_log_mul_log_one_sub_zero","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L223-L238","doc":"`log x · log (1-x) → 0` as `x → 0⁺`. The corpus proves this at `x → 1⁻`; the\nexpression is invariant under `x ↦ 1 - x`, so it transports. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.mem_Ioo_nhdsWithin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.mem_Ioo_nhdsWithin","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L218-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.abelAux_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.abelAux_eq","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L204-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.hasDerivAt_abelAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.hasDerivAt_abelAux","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L169-L200","doc":"**The derivative vanishes.** Every `log` the chain rule produces splits into\n`log x, log (1-x), log y, log (1-y), log (1-xy)`; after that the whole expression\nis a linear form in those five with rational coefficients, and each coefficient\nis identically zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.abelAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.abelAux","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L164-L167","doc":"The five-term expression, as a function of `x` with `y` held fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.hasDerivAt_inner_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.hasDerivAt_inner_right","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L150-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.hasDerivAt_inner_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.hasDerivAt_inner_left","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L139-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.log_one_sub_inner_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.log_one_sub_inner_right","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L131-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.log_inner_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.log_inner_right","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L124-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.log_one_sub_inner_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.log_one_sub_inner_left","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L118-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.log_inner_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.log_inner_left","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L111-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.inner_right_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.inner_right_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L98-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.inner_right_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.inner_right_pos","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L94-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.inner_left_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.inner_left_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L87-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.inner_left_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.inner_left_pos","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L83-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.one_sub_inner_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.one_sub_inner_right","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L76-L81","doc":"The right inner argument's complement: `1 - y(1-x)/(1-xy) = (1-y)/(1-xy)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.one_sub_inner_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.one_sub_inner_left","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L70-L74","doc":"The left inner argument's complement: `1 - x(1-y)/(1-xy) = (1-x)/(1-xy)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.one_sub_mul_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.one_sub_mul_pos","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoAbelFiveTerm.lean#L66-L68","doc":"`1 - x·y > 0` on the square — the denominator every inner argument shares. ","signatureChunk":0}]}